@TITLE Tutorial Dungeon
@AUTHOR picoReader Team
@START entrance
@DESC_TEXT A short tutorial exercising all engine features.

@ROOM entrance
@DESC
You stand before a moss-covered stone
archway. Torchlight flickers from within.
A brass sign reads "DUNGEON OF LEARNING".
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Enter the dungeon" -> foyer
@CHOICE "Read the sign closely" -> entrance_sign

@ROOM entrance_sign
@DESC
The sign reads: "Adventurer! Within these
halls you will learn to explore, collect
items, and make choices. Good luck!"
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET read_sign
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Enter the dungeon" -> foyer

@ROOM foyer
@DESC
A circular chamber with three doors.
Torches line the walls. The air smells
of damp stone and old parchment.
@IF read_sign
You notice scratch marks on the north
door, as if something clawed at it.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@ITEM rusty_key "Rusty Key" "A heavy iron key with teeth worn smooth by age."
@CHOICE "Go north" -> guard_room
@CHOICE "Go east" -> library
@CHOICE "Go west" -> storeroom
@CHOICE "Go back outside" -> entrance

@ROOM storeroom
@DESC
Dusty shelves line the walls. Most are
empty, but you spot a few useful items
among the cobwebs.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM torch "Torch" "A sturdy wooden torch soaked in pitch. It burns brightly."
@ITEM healing_herb "Healing Herb" "A sprig of green herb with a minty smell."
@CHOICE "Search deeper" -> storeroom_back
@CHOICE "Return to foyer" -> foyer

@ROOM storeroom_back
@DESC
Behind a fallen shelf you find a small
leather pouch. Inside is a smooth blue
gemstone that seems to glow faintly.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM blue_gem "Blue Gem" "A perfectly round sapphire that pulses with inner light."
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Return to storeroom" -> storeroom

@ROOM library
@DESC
Tall bookshelves stretch to the ceiling.
A reading desk holds an open tome.
Most books have crumbled to dust.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Read the open tome" -> library_tome
@CHOICE "Search the shelves" -> library_shelves
@CHOICE "Return to foyer" -> foyer

@ROOM library_tome
@DESC
The tome describes an ancient treasure
hidden in the dungeon's depths. It says:
"Only the bearer of three gems may claim
the Dragon's Hoard."
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET know_secret
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Keep reading" -> library
@CHOICE "Return to foyer" -> foyer

@ROOM library_shelves
@DESC
Most books are ruined. Behind a false
panel you find a hidden compartment.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM red_gem "Red Gem" "A ruby that flickers like a tiny flame."
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Return to library" -> library

@ROOM guard_room
@DESC
A stone golem blocks the passage north.
Its eyes glow with a dim red light.
It does not move, but watches you.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Try to sneak past" -> guard_fail
@CHOICE "Offer the healing herb" -> guard_pass @NEED healing_herb
@CHOICE "Return to foyer" -> foyer

@ROOM guard_fail
@DESC
The golem swats you back effortlessly.
You land in a heap by the doorway.
Perhaps it wants something?
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Try again" -> guard_room
@CHOICE "Return to foyer" -> foyer

@ROOM guard_pass
@DESC
You hold out the healing herb. The golem
takes it gently, crushes it, and rubs the
paste on a crack in its stone arm.
It steps aside with a grinding bow.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Proceed north" -> dark_hall @USE healing_herb @SET golem_passed
@SCORE +15

@ROOM dark_hall
@DESC
The passage is pitch black. You can hear
dripping water and distant echoes.
@IF torch
Your torch illuminates rough-hewn walls
and a narrow staircase leading down.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Descend the stairs" -> deep_chamber @NEED torch
@CHOICE "Feel along the wall" -> dark_hall_grope @NEED !torch
@CHOICE "Go back" -> guard_room

@ROOM dark_hall_grope
@DESC
You stumble in the darkness and crack
your shin on a stone step. You need
a light source to proceed safely.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go back for a torch" -> guard_room

@ROOM deep_chamber
@DESC
A vast underground chamber opens before
you. In the center, a stone pedestal
holds a green gemstone.
Ancient carvings cover the walls.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM green_gem "Green Gem" "An emerald that hums with quiet power."
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Examine the carvings" -> deep_carvings
@CHOICE "Go to the vault door" -> vault_door
@CHOICE "Go back upstairs" -> dark_hall

@ROOM deep_carvings
@DESC
The carvings depict a dragon guarding a
mountain of gold. Three gem-shaped slots
are carved around a door at the far end
of the chamber.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET seen_carvings
@CHOICE "Go to the vault door" -> vault_door
@CHOICE "Return" -> deep_chamber

@ROOM vault_door
@DESC
A massive iron door with three gem-shaped
recesses. The slots glow faintly: one
blue, one red, one green.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Place all three gems" -> treasure_room @NEED blue_gem @NEED red_gem @NEED green_gem
@CHOICE "Try to force the door" -> vault_force
@CHOICE "Go back" -> deep_chamber

@ROOM vault_force
@DESC
The door doesn't budge. Not even a
scratch. Whatever magic holds it shut
is far beyond brute strength.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Return" -> vault_door

@ROOM treasure_room
@DESC
The door swings open with a rumble. Gold
coins cascade from overflowing chests.
Jeweled crowns and ancient weapons gleam
in your torchlight. You've found the
Dragon's Hoard!
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +50
@WIN "You claimed the Dragon's Hoard! A true adventurer."

@ROOM pit_trap
@DESC
The floor gives way beneath you! You
tumble into a deep pit with no way out.
The last thing you see is the torch
sputtering in the dust far above.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "You fell into a pit trap. The dungeon claims another soul."
